   502	For a global plane-curve control of the singularity type, the polynomial map
   503	
   504	```text
   505	s |-> (s^2, s(s^2-1))
   506	```
   507	
   508	is immersive and identifies `s=1` with `s=-1`.  Its image
   509	
   510	```text
   511	Y^2=X(X-1)^2
   512	```
   513	
   514	has an ordinary node at `(1,0)` and one point at infinity.  This only shows
   515	that an immersive polynomial normalization can have the required
   516	self-identification; it is not an asymptotic curve of a constructed Keller
