   538	Equations (5.3) and (5.5) then hold on the companion sheets, while the fibre
   539	partition is exactly `(2,1,1)`.  Both companions can therefore belong to the
   540	same special ruling fibre without changing the quartic packet.
   541	
   542	The companion equality locus is `u^mu-v^mu=0`.  For some parities and
   543	relative branch positions it can contain the local branch `B`; otherwise it
   544	merely crosses `B`.  Neither case changes the geometric fibre lengths.
