   546	### 5.3 The charged cusp and node packets
   547	
   548	The standard cubic-discriminant algebra gives the cusp control.  For
   549	`R=C[[s,w]]`, let
   550	
   551	```text
   552	S_c=R[z]/(z^3-3s*z-2w)  times R.                        (5.6)
   553	```
   554	
   555	Its discriminant is a nonzero scalar times `s^3-w^2`.  At the cusp origin
