   576	
   577	## 6. Why `K_U~0` and adjunction do not close the horn
   578	
   579	Restrict the divisor relation (2.2) to `Phi`.  Since `Phi=A1`,
   580	
   581	```text
   582	Pic(Phi)=0,
   583	O_U(Phi)|Phi isomorphic to O_Phi,
   584	O_U(E)|Phi isomorphic to O_Phi.                         (6.1)
   585	```
   586	
   587	Adjunction gives the same result:
   588	
   589	```text
   590	omega_Phi isomorphic to (omega_U tensor O_U(Phi))|Phi
   591	             isomorphic to O_Phi.                      (6.2)
   592	```
   593	
   594	The section cutting out `E intersect Phi` is therefore a polynomial section
   595	of a trivial line bundle on `A1`.  Such a section may have any finite
   596	effective zero divisor; its balancing pole lies at the missing point at
   597	infinity.  In particular, the at-least-two collision points do not conflict
   598	with (6.1)--(6.2).  A projective intersection number cannot be imported
   599	without the boundary terms of a chosen completion.
   600	
   601	There is an analogous canonical firewall for the primitive quartic order.
   602	The scheme
   603	
   604	```text
   605	X=Spec(O(V)[Z]/(P_t)) subset V times A1
   606	```
   607	
   608	is a hypersurface and hence Gorenstein.  Its normalization is finite etale
   609	over `V`, so both sides have locally trivial dualizing modules.  Finite
   610	duality identifies the relative dual fractional ideal with the normalized
   611	dualizing module; after the displayed trivializations that fractional ideal
   612	is principal.  This does not say that the order is normal or that its
   613	conductor is the unit ideal.
   614	The split model (5.1)--(5.3) realizes a nonempty square index divisor while
   615	both normalized sheets have trivial canonical module.
   616	
   617	Finally, `T=div_U(b o pi)` is principal and has trivial dualizing sheaf by
   618	adjunction, exactly as in the producer.  Neither (2.4) nor (6.2) introduces
   619	`b`, so `K_U~0` supplies no new congruence for
   620	`N=#(T intersect Phi)` and does not select either row of (3.7).
   621	
   622	## 7. Maximum-safe conclusion and next gate
   623	
   624	Promote, conditional on the provisional producer, exactly the following.
   625	
   626	> **Inverse-Kummer and primitive-quartic control.**  The residual divisor in
   627	> `pi^*C_0=Phi+E` has class `-[Phi]`, and the regular function
   628	> `r=(c_0 o pi)^mu/(t-a)` has divisor `mu E`.  Its Kummer extension is the
   629	> original cyclic extension, not an independent one.  On the two polynomial
   630	> sources this is the exact factorization (0.3)--(0.4).  Formanek's theorem
   631	> makes `t` a primitive generator of `C(U)/C(A2)`.  The same-fibre collision
   632	> therefore forces a monogenic index/coincidence divisor, locally
   633	> `u^mu-v^mu=0`, but not ramification of `pi` or a bad fibre of `rho`.
   634	> Trivial canonical class and the local quartic `(2,1,1)`, `(3,1)`, and
   635	> `(2,2)` algebras are compatible with this configuration.
   636	
   637	Do not promote any of the following:
   638	
   639	1. `[E]` is independent of `[Phi]`, or `mu^2|d_1`;
   640	2. `E` is irreducible, `r` is an `A1`-fibration, or `E` is another fibre of
   641	   `rho`;
   642	3. the self-identification is transverse, or the roots in (3.6) are simple;
   643	4. the monogenic index divisor is a branch/nonproper divisor of `pi` or `H`;
   644	5. `t` extends regularly over the ramification boundary `R`;
   645	6. the completed-local controls glue to a global cover or a Keller map;
   646	7. `K_U~0` makes `E intersect Phi` empty or fixes its degree.
   647	
   648	The cheapest genuine closing moves are now sharply separated.
   649	
   650	1. **Index-at-infinity gate.**  Prove that the forced coincidence divisor of
   651	   the primitive quartic order contributes a positive Orevkov--Chau boundary
   652	   correction.  Since the producer's budget is saturated, one positive unit
   653	   would contradict the horn.  The missing theorem must distinguish index
   654	   of `O(V)[t]` from ramification of its etale normalization.
   655	2. **Second-fibration gate.**  Use the global pseudo-plane geometry to prove
   656	   that a regular function with `div(r)=mu E`, where `[E]=-[Phi]` and
   657	   `E intersect Phi` contains the collision points, has general fibre `A1`.
   658	   Only then could uniqueness of the `A1`-ruling force a relation with `t`.
   659	3. **Companion-resultant gate.**  Combine the norm identity (4.6) with the
   660	   actual polynomial `q_H=b o H` to force the index divisor to meet `B` at
   661	   the cusp or node, rather than at an allowed ordinary point or only at
   662	   infinity.  The existing Euler identity alone does not do this.
   663	
   664	For the charged strict-block horn, `d_1>=2` and the producer conditionally
   665	gives `mu=d_1` after minimal-degree replacement.  The `d_1=1` pseudo-plane
   666	row is empty already because `mu>=2` and `mu|d_1`.  This says nothing about
   667	an arbitrary canonical rank-four normalization outside the charged
   668	pseudo-plane package; no `d_1=1` specialization is made here.
   669	
   670	No replay is attached.  The new statements are divisor identities, field
   671	tower arithmetic, and exact completed-local algebra formulas valid for all
   672	`mu`; sampling finitely many values would not verify the theorem-level
   673	steps.
