    61	T=U times_(A2) B,          A=T intersect Phi,
    62	N=#A,                      D=V(q)=f_mu^(-1)(T).
    63	```
    64	
    65	Then `A` is finite and
    66	
    67	```text
    68	e(D)=-3mu-(mu-1)N,              D intersect {x=0}=A.     (0.5)
    69	```
    70	
    71	If `nu` is the generic number of points of a vertical fibre of `D`, and one
    72	representative is chosen from every nonzero `mu`-th-root orbit of exceptional
    73	`x`-values, then
    74	
    75	```text
    76	sum_representatives (nu-#D_x)=N+3.                       (0.6)
    77	```
    78	
    79	Thus a nonzero exceptional companion-incidence value is forced, but all
    80	scheme fibres of the ambient `x`-ruling can remain affine lines.  A uniform
    81	polynomial family in Section 6 realizes (0.5)--(0.6), one cusp orbit, no node,
    82	and no bad ruling fibre.  It blocks a purely polynomial-fibre contradiction.
    83	
    84	Indeed, if `r` is the number of irreducible components of `B`, the boundary
    85	over them consumes at least `2mu*r+mu` units (generic length `2mu` on each
    86	component plus the unique cusp increment `mu`), while the `mu-1` deleted
    87	cyclic fibre lines consume at least `mu-1`.  The Orevkov--Chau degree-at-
    88	infinity formula gives
    89	
    90	```text
    91	4mu-1 >= 2mu*r+2mu-1.                                   (0.7)
    92	```
    93	
    94	Thus `r=1`, and equality holds throughout.  The budget is saturated, not
    95	violated.  The node is budget-free because it is a two-point normalization
    96	identification; the forced singularity of `C0` is budget-free for the same
    97	reason.  Hence the function pair gives a sharp new normalization, target-
    98	irreducibility, and collision theorem, not yet an exclusion of
    99	`R4-CYCLE-1`.
